Task 6. Removed "Mexico wedding coordination in Cancun & Riviera Maya"
from sitewide metadata and set the global description to the exact text
specified in the brief.

- app/layout.tsx: global description and og:description replaced. Added
  twitter:description (and twitter:title), which did not exist — the
  brief requires the matching twitter description, and without an
  explicit one Twitter falls back to the page description.
- app/page.tsx: homepage description aligned to the same copy; keywords
  reworked off Mexico/Cancun onto wedding-party outfitting.
- lib/seo.tsx buildLocalBusinessSchema(): description replaced and the
  three Mexico offers dropped from hasOfferCatalog. layout.tsx injects
  this schema on every page, so it is global metadata by any reasonable
  reading of the task.

Mexico remains as body content on the dedicated Mexico landing pages,
/services/, /pricing/ and /about/ — the brief explicitly permits it
outside global metadata.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit exit 0.
